  "id": "COMPOUND:295 - PROTEIN:5306",
  "verbalization": "Mitomycin is linked to NCI-H1770 through a series of molecular interactions, with the most direct pathway involving the bromodomain-containing protein 4, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18. This protein is also a target of mitomycin, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The second pathway connects mitomycin to A388, which in turn targets a complex chemical compound that ultimately affects NCI-H1770. The third pathway links mitomycin to ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, which is also targeted by palmarumycin CP18, reinforcing the role of this enzyme in the interaction. The evidence suggests that mitomycin may influence NCI-H1770 through multiple molecular intermediates, potentially via the modulation of bromodomain-containing proteins or through the action of palmarumycin CP18. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which mitomycin exerts its effects on NCI-H1770, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
